  the local slope runs from 0.76 (outer, dust-dominated) to 0.90 (inner, phantom cusp):
  the composite NEVER flattens: -d ln I/d ln b in [0.7, 1.0) inside r_M, steepening INWARD toward the phantom b^-1 cusp (approaching 1.0 only at depth where the r^-2 phantom wins; the pure phantom alone is EXACTLY 1.0 at every b).
